{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/275296-special-moons-and-uratha","id":275296,"title":"Special Moons and Uratha","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-08T03:08:28-07:00","id":275296,"title":"Special Moons and Uratha","content":"Yesterday was one of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Full_moon#Harvest_and_Hunter.27s_moons\" target=\"_blank\">special Moons of the year</a>, <b>Hunter's Moon</b>. From India's tradition it's best night for hunting. I'm interested are there any specific Moons of the year that Uratha mentions as more special than typical Auspice? What about <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lunar_eclipse\" target=\"_blank\">Red Moon</a>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T06:44:34-07:00","id":275431,"title":"","content":"They're all in Signs of the Moon. The only one that comes to my mind right now is the Gishtahu - Feasting Killer - Changed under the Harvest Moon. They're basically Rahu, their Rage is tainted with an unholy appetite for forbidden flesh - that of Man, Wolf, and Uratha. They lose the Warrior's Eye, but gain the ability to reap an extra mote of Essence should they feed the Hunger. Purity also stops being their Auspice Renown, but they can choose any from the other four instead.<br /> <br /> I remember this because a Gishtahu PC played a very prominent role in a tabletop game I ran in 2010. Needless to say, he'd be a very powerful Elder Zi'ir prowling the Hisil in my games' shared universe by now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T07:12:41-07:00","id":275445,"title":"","content":"And the one last night would be quite auspicious (ha ha, see what I did there?) as it was not only the Blood Moon (see above for Gishthau), but a Lunar Eclipse as well, which is a Suharrahu, the Trickster Warrior. Quote from the book: &quot;The Suharrahu should strike first, strike in the most advantageous spot, and guarantee minimal casualties on her side in all cases.&quot; Auspice Ability is a -3 penalty to everyone else while trying to notice or remember them, including any ambushes, dirty tricks, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T07:24:47-07:00","id":275449,"title":"","content":"I had a character based upon the Lunar Eclipse Blood Moon. He was pretty awesome...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T07:38:53-07:00","id":275451,"title":"","content":"I remember thinking those should be more sinister after the Eclipse gift, but it does seem appropriate for the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}